WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.348
It snowed all night.

2
00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:14.021
The snow piled higher and higher.

3
00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:16.392
First, it covered the grass.

4
00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:18.782
Then, it covered the bushes.

5
00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:22.766
By morning, it even covered the cars.

6
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:27.452
"Rich and Paul! No school today!" called Mom.

7
00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:30.465
"Did you hear that?" Rich asked his brother.

8
00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:37.644
"Wow, no school!" shouted Paul.

9
00:00:37.645 --> 00:00:40.552
Rich and Paul love snow days.

10
00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:42.852
They don't have to go to school.

11
00:00:42.853 --> 00:00:45.284
Snow days are never boring.

12
00:00:45.285 --> 00:00:51.292
There are so many things to do.

13
00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:54.533
First, Paul and Rich make snow angels.

14
00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.880
They find a place in the snow with no footprints.

15
00:00:57.881 --> 00:01:03.611
Carefully, Rich and Paul lie down in the snow.

16
00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:05.939
"Spread your arms and legs.

17
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.780
Move them up and down like this," says Rich.

18
00:01:09.781 --> 00:01:14.061
When they stand up, they can see angel shapes in the snow.

19
00:01:14.062 --> 00:01:18.698
"Ha-ha-ha!" they laugh.

20
00:01:18.699 --> 00:01:22.379
Next, Paul and Rich decide to go sledding.

21
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.550
They both have a fast sled.

22
00:01:27.551 --> 00:01:30.287
"Let's race," says Rich.

23
00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:33.811
"Sure! Are you ready?" says Paul.

24
00:01:33.812 --> 00:01:37.335
"Ready, set, go!"

25
00:01:37.336 --> 00:01:39.314
They race down the hill.

26
00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:46.251
They go faster and faster: "Aaaaaaaah!"

27
00:01:46.252 --> 00:01:49.256
"I'm the winner," says Paul.

28
00:01:49.257 --> 00:01:54.051
"Do you want to go one more time?"

29
00:01:54.052 --> 00:01:58.755
"No, I declare war!" yells Rich.

30
00:01:58.756 --> 00:02:00.974
"Wait!" shouts Paul.

31
00:02:00.975 --> 00:02:03.360
Rich hits Paul with a snowball.

32
00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:06.579
"I'm not ready," says Paul.

33
00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:10.196
Rich hits Paul with another snowball.

34
00:02:10.197 --> 00:02:12.183
They have a snowball fight.

35
00:02:12.184 --> 00:02:15.525
Rich and Paul hit each other with many snowballs.

36
00:02:15.526 --> 00:02:17.599
They get covered in snow.

37
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.423
Then Rich hits Paul with a really big snowball.

38
00:02:21.424 --> 00:02:24.302
It is a fun war.

39
00:02:24.303 --> 00:02:27.780
"Do you want a truce?" Rich asks.

40
00:02:27.781 --> 00:02:31.133
"Okay, truce. What's next?"

41
00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:33.879
"How about building a snowman?"

42
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:37.714
"Sounds great!" says Paul.

43
00:02:37.715 --> 00:02:41.274
Rich and Paul roll a very large snowball.

44
00:02:41.275 --> 00:02:44.535
Then they roll a medium-size snowball.

45
00:02:44.536 --> 00:02:47.102
They lift it on top for the body.

46
00:02:47.103 --> 00:02:49.931
The boys roll a small snowball.

47
00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:54.070
Then they put it on top for the snowman's head.

48
00:02:54.071 --> 00:02:56.644
Rich gets coal from the garage.

49
00:02:56.645 --> 00:03:00.507
Paul runs into the house and gets a carrot and a hat.

50
00:03:00.508 --> 00:03:04.903
They give their snowman eyes, a mouth, and a nose.

51
00:03:04.904 --> 00:03:07.744
Mom comes out to see the snowman.

52
00:03:07.745 --> 00:03:10.579
"Look, Mom! We built a snowman.

53
00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.045
What do you think?" says Paul.

54
00:03:13.046 --> 00:03:15.900
"It's great!" Mom says.

55
00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:18.314
"You have played for a long time.

56
00:03:18.315 --> 00:03:22.301
It's time to come in now."

57
00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:27.087
The boys go into the house and take off their jackets and scarves.

58
00:03:27.088 --> 00:03:29.960
Then they sit by the fire to warm up.

59
00:03:29.961 --> 00:03:33.992
"I hope it snows again tonight," says Rich.

60
00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:38.606
"Another snow day would be great!" agrees Paul.
